==English==
{{was wotd|2006|December|3}}
{{wp|+ organism}}

===Etymology===
{{bor+|en|la|fastīdiōsus||passive: that feels disgust, disdainful, scornful, fastidious; active: that causes disgust, disgusting, loathsome}}, from {{m|la|fastīdium||a loathing, aversion, disgust, niceness of taste, daintiness, etc.}}, perhaps for *''fastutidium'', from {{m|la|fastus||disdain, haughtiness, arrogance, disgust}} + {{m|la|taedium||disgust}}. Cf. {{cog|fr|fastidieux}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|en|/fæsˈtɪdi.əs/|/fəsˈtɪdi.əs/}}
* {{audio|en|en-us-fastidious.ogg|a=US}}
* {{audio|en|en-au-fastidious.ogg|a=AU}}
* {{rhymes|en|ɪdiəs|s=4}}
* {{hyph|en|fas|ti|di|ous}}

===Adjective===
{{en-adj}}

# Excessively [[particular]], [[demand]]ing, or [[fussy]] about details, especially about [[tidiness]] and [[cleanliness]].
#: {{syn|en|exacting|fussy|meticulous|niggly|pernickety|Thesaurus:fastidious}}
# Overly concerned about [[tidiness]] and [[cleanliness]].
# [[difficult|Difficult]] to [[please]]; [[quick]] to find [[fault]].
#* {{RQ:James Portrait|passage=You're too '''fastidious''', and too indolent, and too rich.}}
# {{senseid|en|microbiology}} {{lb|en|microbiology|of a [[microorganism]]}} Having precise requirements for nutrition and environment (chemical and physical); especially, being difficult to [[culture#Verb|culture]] because of those requirements.
#: {{collocation|en|'''fastidious''' organism}}
#: {{collocation|en|'''fastidious''' species}}

